  "_notes": [
    "game_state added locally, from a 4-player game driven through the cabinet's streamer.",
    "current_player and current_ball are adjacent in CPU RAM at 0x00032AB8 and 0x00032AB9, player low",
    "and ball high, the shape every Stern SAM game measured uses.",
    "Scores are 4 bytes on 4-byte centres from 0x021109E4. The sweep also offered 0x00036470 in CPU",
    "RAM, reading 251,000 / 250,500 / 250,500 / 251,500 -- four plausible, evenly spaced, monotonic",
    "values, and wrong. Scores are in NVRAM on every SAM game measured, which is what rejects it.",
    "player_count at 0x02110900, the one address every SAM game shares.",
    "Free Play measured directly: toggled in the operator menu with NVRAM captured either side. The",
    "value goes 1 -> 0 and its check byte 0xFE -> 0xFF, equal and opposite.",
    "It is one record of the 8-byte adjustment array at 0x02102008, where each record is a 32-bit",
    "little-endian value followed by a byte holding 0xFF minus the sum of the value's four bytes.",
    "Writing this field requires updating that check byte, or the game discards the change on reload.",
    "The check byte is declared with an explicit checksum address. Without one, a checksum8",
    "record means the checksum occupies the tail of start..end, which is not this layout: here",
    "the summed bytes and the check byte are separate fields of one record.",
    "ball_count and max_credits are derived, not measured on this game: on every Stern SAM game",
    "measured they sit three and one records below free_play in the adjustment array, a rule",
    "confirmed by menu changes with distinctive values on both array layouts (st_162h and trn_174h).",
    "At the derived addresses this game's image reads the factory defaults, 3 balls and 30 credits,",
    "with valid check bytes. Writing either field requires updating its check byte.",
    "checksum16 declared for all twelve champion records: 32-byte records, initials at +0, score at",
    "+0x18 (Best Combo keeps a 1-byte counter at +0x1A instead), little-endian checksum16 at +28 as",
    "0xFFFF minus the sum of the first 28 bytes -- start..length 30 covers the summed bytes plus the",
    "checksum. All twelve validate against a captured NVRAM image.",
    "game_over, tilted and credits come from a 1,099-frame recording of live memory spanning an",
    "operator-menu session and a full game with a mid-ball tilt on ball 1. The session also promoted",
    "ball_count and max_credits from derived to measured: menu values 5 and 9 landed at adjustment",
    "indices 32 and 34 as the free_play-relative rule predicted.",
    "0x00032AEA is the status bitfield most SAM games keep at ball+0x31, in trn_174h's exact",
    "encoding: 1 in attract, 19 (0x13) in play, 21 (0x15) for the eighteen samples between the tilt",
    "and the end of the tilted ball, during which player 1's score sat frozen at 138,820. game_over",
    "(mask 0x12, inverted) is correct in all 1,099 frames; tilted is bit 0x04.",
    "credits at 0x0211100C, the sixteenth SAM game at that address: rose to 9 with the coins (capped",
    "by the Maximum Credits just set) and fell to 8 at game start."
  ]
